2025-07-11 11:28:00 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 5: 数据 = {'id': 'fbe6c819-43e4-4888-bfb3-ad1620fe9db7', 'document_id': 'f91ead2a-6f87-456f-b5ca-aba2506657d0', 'content': 'resins, tannins, waxes, inorganic salts. At the Geopolymer Laboratory of the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign (UIUC), USA, before utilization the bamboo fibers were washed with deionized water and set to dry-in two layers of paper towels. ![01973e1a-dfe2-7052-97bf-a3fb626b5a97_2_151_1414_987_193_0.jpg](images/01973e1a-dfe2-7052-97bf-a3fb626b5a97_2_151_1414_987_193_0.jpg) Figure 1. Green bamboo (a) culms, (b) chips and (c) fiber bundles. ## Geopolymer Composite\nPotassium silicate solution (or potassium water glass) was made by mixing fumed silica (Cab-O-Sil EH-5 Cabot Corp, Tuscola, IL) with potassium hydroxide pellets (Fisher Scientific Waltham, MA, USA) dissolved in deionized water according to the reaction:\n$$ 2\\mathrm{{KOH}} + {10}{\\mathrm{H}}_{2}0 + 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} \\rightarrow {\\mathrm{K}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} \\cdot 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} \\cdot {11}{\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} \\tag{1} $$\nGeopolymer was prepared at the Geopolymer Laboratory by mixing potassium water glass and Metamax ${}^{\\circledR }$ metakaolin $\\left( {{\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3} \\cdot 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}}\\right)$ (particle size ${1.3\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ ) mixed with a high shear mixer for 5 minutes at ${1100}\\mathrm{{rpm}}$ to obtain good mixing of the components. This slurry was then put in a planetary conditioning mixer that further mixed and degassed for removal of fine bubbles. The geopolymerization reaction can be summed up as follows:\n## ${\\mathrm{K}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} \\cdot 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} \\cdot {11}{\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} + 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} \\cdot {\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3} \\rightarrow {\\mathrm{K}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} \\cdot {\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3} \\cdot 4{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} \\cdot {11}{\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{O}$\n(2)', 'chunk_index': 5, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
