2025-07-11 11:55:11 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 3: 数据 = {'id': '4e475421-52f9-4be6-a657-4a62af8c53d9', 'document_id': '4ccd1965-ac8b-478a-be4a-e82f5229c469', 'content': 'strength ${}^{17}$ . Potassium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${6.4}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ rice stem yielded ${18.45}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ three-point flexure strength ${}^{18}$ . Potassium-based geopolymer reinforced with 30 wt% alkali-treated fique fibers yielded ${11.4}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{19}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${5.5}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ of unidirectional untreated malva resulted in ${31.5}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{20}$ .  Presently, we found no published work on metakaolin-based geopolymer reinforced with bamboo fibers.', 'chunk_index': 3, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
