2025-07-11 14:20:17 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 7: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 14:20:17 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 7: 数据 = {'id': 'b707714c-9adf-4103-a565-1621fa701187', 'document_id': '86b265a7-bbbb-4661-8c50-f4da9fbcd61e', 'content': 'rank $i$ from 1 to $\\mathrm{n}$ , which is the number of samples in the batch. The Weibull distribution function is given by equation (4), where $\\mathrm{v}$ is the non-dimensional volume, $\\sigma$ is the stress, ${\\sigma }_{0}$ is the scale parameter and $m$ is the shape parameter or Weibull modulus: $$ F = 1 - {e}^{\\left\\lbrack -v{\\left( \\frac{\\sigma }{{\\sigma }_{o}}\\right) }^{m}\\right\\rbrack } \\tag{4} $$\nSince the gauge length was the same in all samples, $v = 1$ . In order to determine the Weibull parameters, equation (4) can be rearranged to obtain the following equation:\n$$ \\ln \\left\\lbrack {\\ln \\left( \\frac{1}{1 - F}\\right) }\\right\\rbrack = m\\ln \\left( \\sigma \\right) - m\\ln \\left( {\\sigma }_{0}\\right) \\tag{5} $$\nThis is of the slope-intercept form of a straight line, so $\\ln \\left\\lbrack {\\ln \\left( \\frac{1}{1 - F}\\right) }\\right\\rbrack$ is then plotted versus $\\ln \\left( \\sigma \\right)$ , using the approximation of $\\mathrm{F}$ given in equation (3), and a linear fit is applied for each data series. The slope of the fitted line then corresponds to the Weibull modulus, $m$ , and the $y$ -intercept corresponds to $- m\\ln \\left( {\\sigma }_{0}\\right)$ , which can be solved for the scale parameter, ${\\sigma }_{0}$ . The average value ${\\sigma }_{\\mathrm{f}}$ can be calculated according to the equation (6), where $\\Gamma$ is the gamma function:\n$$ {\\sigma }_{f} = {\\sigma }_{0}\\sqrt{\\Gamma \\left( {1 + \\frac{1}{m}}\\right) } \\tag{6} $$\nThe standard deviation, $S$ , was calculated using the following equation:\n$$ S = {\\sigma }_{0}\\sqrt{\\Gamma \\left( {1 + \\frac{2}{m}}\\right) - {\\left\\lbrack \\Gamma \\left( 1 + \\frac{1}{m}\\right) \\right\\rbrack }^{2}} \\tag{7} $$\n## Materials Characterization', 'chunk_index': 7, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
