2025-07-11 19:22:21 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 4: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 19:22:21 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 4: 数据 = {'id': '99501ad4-3ad5-4314-ac66-45c7590aa5e2', 'document_id': '861d4601-802f-4bc4-a947-885b3af5da45', 'content': ' Presently, we found no published work on metakaolin-based geopolymer reinforced with bamboo fibers. This is a preliminary research on geopolymer composites reinforced with bamboo fibers. The bamboo-reinforced geopolymer composites are designed as green, sustainable materials, alternative to conventional cements and concretes.\n## MATERIALS AND METHODS\n## Bamboo Fibers\nGuadua angustifolia bamboo species was selected based on abundance, accessibility, mechanical properties and durability. Four-year old bamboo culms were collected from a research plantation area ${}^{{21},{22}}$ at the Brazilian National Institute for Amazonian Research (INPA) in Manaus, Amazonas, Brazil, and immersed in water for three days for better machine workability. The green bamboo culms (Fig. 1(a)) were chopped through a chipper and the chips (Fig. 1(b)) were transformed into fiber bundles (Fig. 1(c)) through a hammer mill. The bamboo fiber bundles were air-dried and filtered by a sifter machine through a mesh #4(12.51 - 40mm), producing short bamboo fibers. The main chemical constituents of bamboo are ${60}\\%$ cellulose and ${32}\\%$ lignin and hemicellulose ${}^{23}$ . Minor constituents are resins, tannins, waxes, inorganic salts. At the Geopolymer Laboratory of the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign (UIUC), USA, before utilization the bamboo fibers were washed with deionized water and set to dry-in two layers of paper towels.\n![01973e1a-dfe2-7052-97bf-a3fb626b5a97_2_151_1414_987_193_0.jpg](images/01973e1a-dfe2-7052-97bf-a3fb626b5a97_2_151_1414_987_193_0.jpg)\nFigure 1. Green bamboo (a) culms, (b) chips and (c) fiber bundles.', 'chunk_index': 4, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
