2025-07-11 19:29:46 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 1: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 19:29:46 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 1: 数据 = {'id': '4cad8b52-2bbf-4f5e-a398-dc33b94973ec', 'document_id': '308caa4d-0411-422e-b38c-baa8fb6a11c1', 'content': 'was carried out according to ASTM standard C1341-13. Scanning electron microscopy was used to investigate the microstructure of the composite materials. X-ray diffraction was used to confirm the formation of geopolymer. Samples of potassium-metakaolin-based geopolymer composites reinforced with bamboo fibers behaved as a potential material for sustainable construction. ## INTRODUCTION Brazil has mineral reserves containing aluminosilicates and many industrial processes that generate fly ash and other by-products as sources of aluminosilicates. Thus, it has the raw material in abundance for exploitation of this technology. The introduction of fibers and particles of native or natural materials grown in the Amazon (such as bamboo) in the production of geopolymeric\nDevelopments in Strategic Ceramic Materials II: A Collection of Papers Presented at the 40th International Conference on Advanced Ceramics and Composites, Volume 37, Issue 7\nEdited by Waltraud M. Kriven, Jingyang Wang, Yanchun Zhou, Dongming Zhu and Gustavo Costa Copyright © 2017 by The American Ceramic Society composites, improve the strength, rigidity, and workability of the final product, generating green high-performance materials. The use of regional and local materials in the production of geopolymeric composites reduce environmental impacts and raise their practicality in different situations.\nNatural fibers have low density, low cost and low energy consumption, as well as neutralizing ${\\mathrm{{CO}}}_{2}$ . Characteristics of bamboo fibers include: low cost, high strength and biodegradability; absorption of ${\\mathrm{{CO}}}_{2}$ and production of ${\\mathrm{O}}_{2}$ three times more than other plants.', 'chunk_index': 1, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
