2025-07-11 19:29:46 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 2: 数据 = {'id': '25ac93ea-6180-40db-bbbd-9cb18c6f31e3', 'document_id': '308caa4d-0411-422e-b38c-baa8fb6a11c1', 'content': 'environmental impacts and raise their practicality in different situations. Natural fibers have low density, low cost and low energy consumption, as well as neutralizing ${\\mathrm{{CO}}}_{2}$ . Characteristics of bamboo fibers include: low cost, high strength and biodegradability; absorption of ${\\mathrm{{CO}}}_{2}$ and production of ${\\mathrm{O}}_{2}$ three times more than other plants. The search for tough and high strength green geopolymer composites led several researchers to use natural fibers, such as basalt ${}^{{13},{14}}$ , corn husk ${}^{15}$ , wool ${}^{16}$ , jute ${}^{17}$ , rice stem ${}^{18}$ , fique ${}^{19}$ , ${\\text{malva}}^{20}$ for reinforcement of metakaolin-based geopolymer. The addition of ${10}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ of ${13\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ diameter x ${6.35}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ long basalt fibers to potassium-based geopolymer composites yielded 19.5 MPa three-point flexure strength ${}^{13}$ . Increasing the chopped basalt fiber length to ${12.7}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ yielded ${27.07}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ three-point flexure strength ${}^{14}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with corn husk fiber bundles resulted in ${14.14}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{15}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with $5\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ wool fiber bundles yielded ${8.1} - {9.1}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ three-point flexure strength ${}^{16}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${30}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ untreated jute weave resulted in ${20.5}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{17}$ . Potassium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${6.4}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ rice stem yielded ${18.45}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ three-point flexure strength ${}^{18}$ . Potassium-based geopolymer reinforced with 30 wt% alkali-treated fique fibers yielded ${11.4}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{19}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${5.5}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ of unidirectional untreated malva resulted in ${31.5}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{20}$ .', 'chunk_index': 2, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
