2025-07-11 19:45:10 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 0: 数据 = {'id': '5fb93f69-f379-49fc-96cf-e550b96afe45', 'document_id': '7266f9ca-00f6-4557-a304-b15b6dfe1de1', 'content': '## Bamboo-Geopolymer Composite: A Preliminary Study: Ceramic Engineering and Science Proceedings Volume 37, Issue 7\n![01973e1a-dfe2-7052-97bf-a3fb626b5a97_0_111_532_1250_678_0.jpg](images/01973e1a-dfe2-7052-97bf-a3fb626b5a97_0_111_532_1250_678_0.jpg)\nRuy A. Sá Ribeiro ${}^{a, b}$ , Marilene G. Sá Ribeiro ${}^{b}$ , Kaushik Sankar ${}^{a}$ , Waltraud M. Kriven ${}^{a}$\n${}^{\\mathrm{a}}$ Department of Materials Science and Engineering, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign, Urbana, IL, USA\n${}^{\\mathrm{b}}$ Structural Engineering Laboratory, National Institute for Amazonian Research, Manaus, AM, Brazil\n## ABSTRACT\nBamboo-reinforced geopolymer composites are intended to be used as sustainable construction materials. A composite was made with potassium-metakaolin geopolymer and reinforced with randomly oriented bamboo fibers from the Amazon region. Bamboo was used in the composition for its potential and viability, as well as very distinguished fast growing characteristics. Four-point flexural strength testing of the geopolymer composite reinforced with bamboo fibers was carried out according to ASTM standard C1341-13. Scanning electron microscopy was used to investigate the microstructure of the composite materials. X-ray diffraction was used to confirm the formation of geopolymer. Samples of potassium-metakaolin-based geopolymer composites reinforced with bamboo fibers behaved as a potential material for sustainable construction.\n## INTRODUCTION', 'chunk_index': 0, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': {'paragraph_index': 0, 'original_length': 115}}}
2025-07-11 19:45:10 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:178 - 分块 0 创建成功: 5fb93f69-f379-49fc-96cf-e550b96afe45
2025-07-11 19:45:10 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 1: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 19:45:10 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 1: 数据 = {'id': 'c949255b-785c-4a29-adba-44da7d36c846', 'document_id': '7266f9ca-00f6-4557-a304-b15b6dfe1de1', 'content': 'was carried out according to ASTM standard C1341-13. Scanning electron microscopy was used to investigate the microstructure of the composite materials. X-ray diffraction was used to confirm the formation of geopolymer. Samples of potassium-metakaolin-based geopolymer composites reinforced with bamboo fibers behaved as a potential material for sustainable construction. ## INTRODUCTION Brazil has mineral reserves containing aluminosilicates and many industrial processes that generate fly ash and other by-products as sources of aluminosilicates. Thus, it has the raw material in abundance for exploitation of this technology. The introduction of fibers and particles of native or natural materials grown in the Amazon (such as bamboo) in the production of geopolymeric\nDevelopments in Strategic Ceramic Materials II: A Collection of Papers Presented at the 40th International Conference on Advanced Ceramics and Composites, Volume 37, Issue 7\nEdited by Waltraud M. Kriven, Jingyang Wang, Yanchun Zhou, Dongming Zhu and Gustavo Costa Copyright © 2017 by The American Ceramic Society composites, improve the strength, rigidity, and workability of the final product, generating green high-performance materials. The use of regional and local materials in the production of geopolymeric composites reduce environmental impacts and raise their practicality in different situations.\nNatural fibers have low density, low cost and low energy consumption, as well as neutralizing ${\\mathrm{{CO}}}_{2}$ . Characteristics of bamboo fibers include: low cost, high strength and biodegradability; absorption of ${\\mathrm{{CO}}}_{2}$ and production of ${\\mathrm{O}}_{2}$ three times more than other plants.', 'chunk_index': 1, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
