2025-07-11 21:33:14 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 2: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:33:14 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 2: 数据 = {'id': 'b6f63221-ba6b-43c1-b89a-950dd0413eb8', 'document_id': 'fd7318ca-a581-4344-bd49-51a66c09650e', 'content': 'environmental impacts and raise their practicality in different situations. Natural fibers have low density, low cost and low energy consumption, as well as neutralizing ${\\mathrm{{CO}}}_{2}$ . Characteristics of bamboo fibers include: low cost, high strength and biodegradability; absorption of ${\\mathrm{{CO}}}_{2}$ and production of ${\\mathrm{O}}_{2}$ three times more than other plants. The search for tough and high strength green geopolymer composites led several researchers to use natural fibers, such as basalt ${}^{{13},{14}}$ , corn husk ${}^{15}$ , wool ${}^{16}$ , jute ${}^{17}$ , rice stem ${}^{18}$ , fique ${}^{19}$ , ${\\text{malva}}^{20}$ for reinforcement of metakaolin-based geopolymer. The addition of ${10}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ of ${13\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ diameter x ${6.35}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ long basalt fibers to potassium-based geopolymer composites yielded 19.5 MPa three-point flexure strength ${}^{13}$ . Increasing the chopped basalt fiber length to ${12.7}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ yielded ${27.07}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ three-point flexure strength ${}^{14}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with corn husk fiber bundles resulted in ${14.14}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{15}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with $5\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ wool fiber bundles yielded ${8.1} - {9.1}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ three-point flexure strength ${}^{16}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${30}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ untreated jute weave resulted in ${20.5}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{17}$ . Potassium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${6.4}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ rice stem yielded ${18.45}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ three-point flexure strength ${}^{18}$ . Potassium-based geopolymer reinforced with 30 wt% alkali-treated fique fibers yielded ${11.4}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{19}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${5.5}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ of unidirectional untreated malva resulted in ${31.5}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{20}$ .', 'chunk_index': 2, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
2025-07-11 21:33:14 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:178 - 分块 2 创建成功: b6f63221-ba6b-43c1-b89a-950dd0413eb8
2025-07-11 21:33:14 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 3: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:33:14 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 3: 数据 = {'id': '184f706e-46c5-45b1-a82a-52d1a184acab', 'document_id': 'fd7318ca-a581-4344-bd49-51a66c09650e', 'content': 'strength ${}^{17}$ . Potassium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${6.4}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ rice stem yielded ${18.45}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ three-point flexure strength ${}^{18}$ . Potassium-based geopolymer reinforced with 30 wt% alkali-treated fique fibers yielded ${11.4}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{19}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${5.5}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ of unidirectional untreated malva resulted in ${31.5}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{20}$ .  Presently, we found no published work on metakaolin-based geopolymer reinforced with bamboo fibers.', 'chunk_index': 3, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
2025-07-11 21:33:14 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:178 - 分块 3 创建成功: 184f706e-46c5-45b1-a82a-52d1a184acab
2025-07-11 21:33:14 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 4: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:33:14 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 4: 数据 = {'id': '2e4117a3-adfd-4532-8a97-4ef17877d1a3', 'document_id': 'fd7318ca-a581-4344-bd49-51a66c09650e', 'content': ' Presently, we found no published work on metakaolin-based geopolymer reinforced with bamboo fibers. This is a preliminary research on geopolymer composites reinforced with bamboo fibers. The bamboo-reinforced geopolymer composites are designed as green, sustainable materials, alternative to conventional cements and concretes.\n## MATERIALS AND METHODS\n## Bamboo Fibers\nGuadua angustifolia bamboo species was selected based on abundance, accessibility, mechanical properties and durability. Four-year old bamboo culms were collected from a research plantation area ${}^{{21},{22}}$ at the Brazilian National Institute for Amazonian Research (INPA) in Manaus, Amazonas, Brazil, and immersed in water for three days for better machine workability. The green bamboo culms (Fig. 1(a)) were chopped through a chipper and the chips (Fig. 1(b)) were transformed into fiber bundles (Fig. 1(c)) through a hammer mill. The bamboo fiber bundles were air-dried and filtered by a sifter machine through a mesh #4(12.51 - 40mm), producing short bamboo fibers. The main chemical constituents of bamboo are ${60}\\%$ cellulose and ${32}\\%$ lignin and hemicellulose ${}^{23}$ . Minor constituents are resins, tannins, waxes, inorganic salts. At the Geopolymer Laboratory of the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign (UIUC), USA, before utilization the bamboo fibers were washed with deionized water and set to dry-in two layers of paper towels.\n![01973e1a-dfe2-7052-97bf-a3fb626b5a97_2_151_1414_987_193_0.jpg](images/01973e1a-dfe2-7052-97bf-a3fb626b5a97_2_151_1414_987_193_0.jpg)\nFigure 1. Green bamboo (a) culms, (b) chips and (c) fiber bundles.', 'chunk_index': 4, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
