2025-07-11 21:33:15 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 5: 数据 = {'id': '3d91cfc1-df82-4763-8da0-84f6737792d0', 'document_id': '0598c657-0b7a-4c72-b91d-55f30607886e', 'content': '(g)</td></tr><tr><td>Large</td><td>38.7</td><td>36.3</td><td>83.9</td></tr><tr><td>Medium</td><td>21.1</td><td>37.6</td><td>25.8</td></tr><tr><td>Small</td><td>12.2</td><td>35.9</td><td>8.4</td></tr></table> After 1 week of curing, the samples were demolded and allowed to bench dry for ${48}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ . Examples of the sample dimensions are shown in Table 2 and Figure 3. Three sizes were chosen to study the scalability and impact of the aspect ratio. ### 2.2 | Heat treatments Sample height, diameter, and weight were recorded using a calliper accurate to $\\pm {0.01}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}$ and weighing scale accurate to $\\pm {0.01}\\mathrm{{mg}}$ before and after heating. Three samples of varying diameter, as shown in Figure 3, were selected for each heat treatment and are summarized in Table 3.\n### 2.3 | Apparent porosity\nThe apparent porosity and density of the samples were found via the Archimedes method as per ASTM C20. ${}^{33}\\mathrm{{RO}}$ water at ${24}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ was used as the reference fluid. Samples were placed in a drying oven at ${110}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for ${24}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ before the dry weight was measured. Next, the samples were placed in boiling water for at least $2\\mathrm{\\;h}$ and allowed to cool to room temperature over ${12}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ . This was done to saturate any open pores with reference fluid.\nSaturated samples were suspended in the reference fluid, and the weight was recorded. The submerged weight reflected the sample weight offset by the buoyant force. Next, samples were removed from the reference fluid. Free surfaces were wiped of excess fluid, and the saturated sample was weighed. Dry, submerged, and saturated weights were then used in Equations (3)-(8) to determine bulk density, grain density, and open porosity.\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_3_155_135_1458_363_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_3_155_135_1458_363_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 3 Side view (left) and top view (right) of cylindrical samples before heating', 'chunk_index': 5, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
