2025-07-11 21:33:15 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 8: 数据 = {'id': '0bc3eeb1-c4e6-4cc4-a439-31e436be54c5', 'document_id': '0598c657-0b7a-4c72-b91d-55f30607886e', 'content': 'any sample. The largest size samples developed a hairline crack after heating to ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ , as shown in Figure 5. ![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_165_134_663_339_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_165_134_663_339_0.jpg) FIGURE 4 Geopolymer samples after heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for $5\\mathrm{\\;h}$ with a heating and cooling rate of ${1}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}/\\mathrm{{min}}$ ![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_184_626_625_303_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_184_626_625_303_0.jpg) FIGURE 5 Geopolymer sample after heating to ${300}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C},{600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ , and ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for $5\\mathrm{\\;h}$ (left to right). Cracking occurred in the largest diameter samples after heating to ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_161_1116_669_565_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_161_1116_669_565_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 6 Linear shrinkage of geopolymer samples due to heat treatment (KGP: potassium metakaolin-based geopolymer)\n### 3.2 | Length and mass changes\nThe dimensional and mass changes accompanying different sintering temperatures were measured experimentally, and the results are summarized in Figures 6 and 7. Changes in length and mass of heat-treated samples were analyzed using Weibull statistics. Weibull analysis provided both an average and variability modulus. A high Weibull modulus indicates low variability. ${}^{34}$\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_906_133_737_621_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_906_133_737_621_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 7 Mass loss of potassium metakaolin-based geopolymer (KGP) composites after heat treatment.\nThe highest amount of length change, $\\sim 7\\%$ , occurred after heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ . Similarly, samples heated to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ varied the most, as seen in Figure 6. The dwell time was not as significant as the target temperature, with the curves for 5and ${20}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ being similar', 'chunk_index': 8, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
