2025-07-11 21:33:15 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 9: 数据 = {'id': '77499330-116d-4ed8-b0c6-f387fb905068', 'document_id': '0598c657-0b7a-4c72-b91d-55f30607886e', 'content': 'highest amount of length change, $\\sim 7\\%$ , occurred after heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ . Similarly, samples heated to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ varied the most, as seen in Figure 6. The dwell time was not as significant as the target temperature, with the curves for 5and ${20}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ being similar Thermal analysis was used to quantify mass loss and phase changes of the sample, if applicable. Figures 10 and 11 summarize significant measurements that were used to calculate glass transition and melting temperatures as well as composite mass loss. The geopolymer composite lost ${5.5}\\%$ mass upon heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ . The glass transition temperature and melting temperature of the glass powder were measured to be ${542}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and ${573}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ , respectively. The glass powder did not undergo any mass loss. The geopolymer composite did not change in phase up to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and is therefore not shown here.\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_5_127_120_740_550_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_5_127_120_740_550_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 8 Apparent bulk density of geopolymer samples measured by ASTM C20 using boiling water (KGP: potassium metakaolin-based geopolymer)\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_5_126_834_737_533_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_5_126_834_737_533_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 9 Open porosity (right) of geopolymer samples measured by ASTM C20 using boiling water (KGP: potassium metakaolin-based geopolymer)\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_5_127_1528_733_519_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_5_127_1528_733_519_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 10 Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) of geopolymer composite (ASH-G: amorphous self-healing geopolymer)', 'chunk_index': 9, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
