2025-07-11 21:33:15 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 10: 数据 = {'id': '073f5af0-a9db-4213-a6a3-1f11af978d73', 'document_id': '0598c657-0b7a-4c72-b91d-55f30607886e', 'content': 'Apparent bulk density of geopolymer samples measured by ASTM C20 using boiling water (KGP: potassium metakaolin-based geopolymer) ![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_5_126_834_737_533_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_5_126_834_737_533_0.jpg) FIGURE 9 Open porosity (right) of geopolymer samples measured by ASTM C20 using boiling water (KGP: potassium metakaolin-based geopolymer) ![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_5_127_1528_733_519_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_5_127_1528_733_519_0.jpg) FIGURE 10 Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) of geopolymer composite (ASH-G: amorphous self-healing geopolymer) Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) micrographs of a specimen before and after heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ are shown in Figure 13. The individual glass and alumina particles were no longer visible at this magnification, and there was a clear development of large pores. These pores were not connected and were therefore considered to be closed porosity, consistent with the porosity measurements made in Figure 9. ImageJ software was used to determine the average closed porosity of samples heated to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for both 5 and ${20}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ , cross-sectioned, polished using $< {5\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ diamond paste and found to be 10 vol%. Samples heated to ${300}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ did not have circular pores, as shown in Figure 14. No differences were observed between samples heated for 5and ${20}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ .\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_6_340_135_1092_410_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_6_340_135_1092_410_0.jpg)\nFIG URE 12 Alumina platelets (left) and glass powder (right) before addition to the potassium metakaolin-based geopolymer (KGP) matrix\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_6_342_713_1090_427_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_6_342_713_1090_427_0.jpg)\nFIG URE 13 Geopolymer composite before (left) and after heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for ${20}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ using heating/cooling rates of ${1}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}/\\mathrm{{min}}$ (right)', 'chunk_index': 10, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
