2025-07-11 21:33:15 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 12: 数据 = {'id': 'a21dd6ce-0168-46f6-805d-18432d56d037', 'document_id': '0598c657-0b7a-4c72-b91d-55f30607886e', 'content': 'of specimens heated to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ were inspected using EDS, as shown in Figure 15. Three distinct phases could be confirmed. The highest aluminium phase was alumina platelets, the phase highest in $\\mathrm{K}$ was leucite, and the third phase with medium amounts of aluminium and potassium was amorphous glass. As shown in Figure 4, a uniform glass glaze developed on samples heated to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ . Samples were cross-sectioned and polished using $< {5\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ diamond paste, and SEM micrographs were analyzed using ImageJ software. Figure 16 shows that the glaze measured using ImageJ had a nominal thickness of ${250\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ .\n### 3.6 | X-ray diffractometry\nX-ray diffraction (XRD) patterns were collected for starting materials, individual phases before and after heating, and amorphous self-healing geopolymer (ASH-G) composites before and after heating. The starting materials were found to be crystalline alpha alumina, amorphous glass, and amorphous geopolymer. The unheated ASH-G composites that were cured at room temperature and not subjected to any sintering treatment were found to be a mixture of individual phases with no chemical reactions taking place, as shown in Figure 17.\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_7_339_134_1096_812_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_7_339_134_1096_812_0.jpg)\nFIG URE 14 Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) micrographs of geopolymer composites using a backscattered electron detector. As cured (A), after exposure to ${300}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ (B), ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ (C), and ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ (D).\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_7_337_1096_1098_526_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_7_337_1096_1098_526_0.jpg)', 'chunk_index': 12, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
