2025-07-11 21:33:15 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 17: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:33:15 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 17: 数据 = {'id': '0356cda5-5c8e-4ba5-84d8-808786dd4b2c', 'document_id': '0598c657-0b7a-4c72-b91d-55f30607886e', 'content': 'increased by a minor amount after heating to ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ , after which the glassy phase began to melt and fill microcracks, thereby drastically increasing the density. The filling of microcracks by the molten glass after heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ eliminated open porosity, as seen in Figure 9. The change from an open nanoporous KGP matrix containing dense particulate phases to a dense glass-leucite matrix containing Oswalt ripened, and closed porosity occurred after slow heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for extended periods. KGP experienced a shift from open porosity to semi-closed porosity after heating to ${850}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C} \\cdot {}^{40}$ The cumulative closed pore area of ASH-G heated to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ was ${10}\\%$ , as shown in Figure 13. The 10% closed porosity was speculated to be due to trapped gaseous species.\nThe XRD data in Figure 19 showed that the geopoly-mer matrix transformed to leucite when heated at ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for extended periods. It has been shown that leucite formation corresponds to a geopolymer linear shrinkage of ${15}\\% {.}^{39}$ This shrinkage may have imparted local pressure on the glass melt, promoting flow of the glass phase into the microcracks within the microstructure. The lack of crystallization in glass heated to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ showed that the glass could repeatedly melt and fill cracks upon heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ . Similarly, the glass glaze can act as a uniform fusing base that can be used to join multiple pieces using localized heat, that is, acetylene torch, infrared heat, etc.', 'chunk_index': 17, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
