2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 1: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 1: 数据 = {'id': '37da5efe-7f48-4779-996d-f2882550510e', 'document_id': '846eec7c-7c34-46ba-806b-aa960ee98a23', 'content': 'in improving rubber properties. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 4\\right\\rbrack }$ Synthetic silicas, for instance precipitated silica, possess siloxane and acidic silanol groups (Si-OH), ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 5\\right\\rbrack }$ and have also been widely used in the polymer industries. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 6\\right\\rbrack }$ Typically the silica surfaces are hydrophilic, so they have strong tendency to adsorb moisture.  ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 7\\right\\rbrack }$ Furthermore, when large amounts of silica are added, the compound viscosity is increased substantially due to strong silica-silica interactions, ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 8\\right\\rbrack }$ and the production of these conventional fillers is highly energy-consuming. Thus, alternative fillers from renewable resources are of considerable interest to improve the properties of rubber while improving sustainability and green aspects of the rubber life cycle.', 'chunk_index': 1, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
