2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 5: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 5: 数据 = {'id': '1d226b8d-6467-47ca-abd8-ca1bf565b0dc', 'document_id': '846eec7c-7c34-46ba-806b-aa960ee98a23', 'content': 'GP-filled NR composites. It was concluded that ${10}\\mathrm{{phr}}$ of GP in NR composites might be suitable for some industrial applications. ## KEYWORDS composites, geopolymer, mechanical properties, natural rubber, thermal properties ## 1 INTRODUCTION ![01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_1_126_130_1011_755_0.jpg](images/01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_1_126_130_1011_755_0.jpg) FIGURE 1 Geopolymerization reactions of fly ash with alkaline solution. $\\mathrm{M} +$ refers to alkali cations Geopolymers (GPs) are polymerized chains or networks of inorganic aluminosilicate molecules linked with covalent bonds. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {19}\\right\\rbrack }$ They are synthesized at room temperature from predominantly silica and aluminum materials of geological origin, or with by-products such as fly ash, as geopolymer-ization process shown in Figure 1. The geopolymers are a comparatively new type of material containing pozzolan components and alkaline solution. It is noted that fly ash has been frequently used as the pozzolan material in the synthesis of GPs. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {20}\\right\\rbrack }$ Therefore, geopolymers can be produced from waste materials and thus reduce environmental problems. In particular, a new and green solution is to utilize fly ash to avoid its negative impacts on environment and ecology, instead trapping the toxic trace metal elements in geopolymer structures. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {21}\\right\\rbrack }$ The fly ash-based geopolymers typically exhibit superior mechanical properties with low density and cage-like crystalline structure. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {19}\\right\\rbrack }$ Furthermore, their durability has been recognized as nearly comparable to that of hydrated Portland cement, and they can be used as green cement. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {22}\\right\\rbrack }$ Geopolymers might also have use as new alternative fillers that improve various properties of rubber composites. This is because geopolymers contain Si and Al ions that could form linkages with organic polymer molecules. Therefore, the geopolymer might interact with the rubber molecules, which enhances reinforcement effects.', 'chunk_index': 5, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
