2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 6: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 6: 数据 = {'id': '2f3bba75-f77c-4c92-a02e-65181f2b070d', 'document_id': '846eec7c-7c34-46ba-806b-aa960ee98a23', 'content': 'cement. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {22}\\right\\rbrack }$ Geopolymers might also have use as new alternative fillers that improve various properties of rubber composites. This is because geopolymers contain Si and Al ions that could form linkages with organic polymer molecules. Therefore, the geopolymer might interact with the rubber molecules, which enhances reinforcement effects.  These might be innovative and advantageous fillers in natural rubber composites. Therefore, the novel NR/GP composites which were prepared in this work had benefit over the conventional fillers in particular low energy-consuming process.', 'chunk_index': 6, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
