2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 17: 数据 = {'id': '6124b361-2ba4-47e5-ac1c-7946c1b75eac', 'document_id': '846eec7c-7c34-46ba-806b-aa960ee98a23', 'content': ' ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {28}\\right\\rbrack }$ The geopolymer formed here consisted of ${30}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ ${\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2},{17.9}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\% \\mathrm{{CaO}},{12.4}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\% {\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ , and other substances (Table 4). Figure 5 shows the cure curves for the gum, and for the NR vulcanizates with various geopolymer loadings or with 10 phr fly ash. It is seen that the torque abruptly increased with the incorporation of ${10}\\mathrm{{phr}}$ geopolymer from that of the gum compound. Furthermore, slight reversion (decreasing trend in torque after its maximum) was observed. This might be attributed to the degradation of di-and polysulfidic linkages that have poor thermal stability in the cross-linked system. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {29}\\right\\rbrack }$ The reversion behavior became more pronounced with ${40}\\mathrm{{phr}}$ of geopolymer due to changes in the cross-linked structure of the vulcanizate after the maximum vulcanization. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {30}\\right\\rbrack }$ Furthermore, lower curing curves were observed with increasing GP loading. This might be due to the formation of larger geopolymer agglomerates with poor distribution in the NR matrix, which hindered the cross-linking reactions and weakened internal strength. Furthermore, it is also seen that the curing curve of the NR compound with ${10}\\mathrm{{phr}}\\mathrm{{FA}}$ was much below the curve for the compound with ${10}\\mathrm{{phr}}\\mathrm{{GP}}$ . This might be attributed to the larger particle size of fly ash (Figure 3), and it gives larger agglomerates with poorer distribution than the GP (Figures 6 and 7). Furthermore, the GP/NR (10 phr) vulcanizate exhibited higher delta torque than the gum NR vulcanizate or the NR/FA (10 phr). This indicates higher cross-link density in the composite with GP.', 'chunk_index': 17, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
