2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 23: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 23: 数据 = {'id': '15facf7f-3a33-42f5-8c9b-aac1b0252771', 'document_id': '846eec7c-7c34-46ba-806b-aa960ee98a23', 'content': '${100}\\%$ modulus and the stress-strain curve from those of the gum NR vulcanizate. This might be due to agglomeration of filler (Figures 6 and 7) which reduced effective specific surface and reinforcing performance. This result agrees well with the high delta torque for the NR composite with ${10}\\mathrm{{phr}}\\mathrm{{GP}}$ (Table 6). The mechanical properties tensile strength and elongation at break, obtained from the failure points of the stress-strain curves in Figure 9, are plotted in Figure 10. It can be seen that the GP/NR (10 phr) vulcanizate exhibited higher tensile strength but lower elongation at break than the gum NR vulcanizate. This may be due to the interactions of geopolymer and NR that improved the strength but reduced the ability to extend. Furthermore, further increase in geopolymer loading decreased the tensile strength and the elongation at break. This again might be due to excessive filler loading creating flaws that initiate failure: voids, cavities, and filler aggregates (Figures 6 and 7). The lack of adhesion between rubber matrix and filler allowed formation of weak spots that degraded tensile strength and elongation at break. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {31}\\right\\rbrack }$\n![01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_8_624_1485_1014_714_0.jpg](images/01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_8_624_1485_1014_714_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 10 Tensile strength and elongation at break for the gum, and for fly ash- or geopolymer-filled natural rubber vulcanizates with various geopolymer loadings or with 10 phr fly ash\nFIGURE 11 Storage modulus as a function of strain amplitude for the gum, and for fly ash- or geopolymer-filled natural rubber vulcanizates with various geopolymer loadings or 10 phr fly ash, tested at ${80}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and $1\\mathrm{\\;{Hz}}$', 'chunk_index': 23, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
