2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:164 - 创建分块 24: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:33:37 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:165 - 创建分块 24: 数据 = {'id': '4b11cef4-b7fe-4e6a-b054-aaf4cca86dfe', 'document_id': '846eec7c-7c34-46ba-806b-aa960ee98a23', 'content': 'rubber vulcanizates with various geopolymer loadings or with 10 phr fly ash FIGURE 11 Storage modulus as a function of strain amplitude for the gum, and for fly ash- or geopolymer-filled natural rubber vulcanizates with various geopolymer loadings or 10 phr fly ash, tested at ${80}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and $1\\mathrm{\\;{Hz}}$ The storage modulus of a filled polymer composite is typically influenced by the interfacial interactions of inorganic filler particles with polymer matrix. Strain-induced filler-filler network breakdown typically occurs during dynamic mechanical experiments at a constant frequency and temperature. Figure 11 shows the storage modulus as a function of strain amplitude for the gum, and the FA- and GP-filled NR vulcanizates with various geopolymer loadings or with ${10}\\mathrm{{phr}}$ fly ash, tested at ${80}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and $1\\mathrm{\\;{Hz}}$ . Nearly linear viscoelastic behavior was observed for the gum NR vulcanizate, whereas nonlinear viscoelastic behavior was seen with both GP/NR and FA/NR composites. This might be attributed to the breakdown of filler-filler networks known as the Payne effect. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {32}\\right\\rbrack }$ It is noted that ${\\mathrm{G}}^{\\prime }$ is a measure of the energy stored/released mechanically during cyclic deformations, and it decreased monotonically with the strain amplitude in all cases. Generally, the absolute value of ${\\mathrm{G}}^{\\prime }$ in the low-strain regime relates to filler-filler networks. It is seen that ${\\mathrm{G}}^{\\prime }$ in the low-strain regime for the GP-filled NR composites increased with filler loading, while the FA-filled NR composite had the lowest value. This implies that the filler-filler networks grew with geopolymer loading while the FA filler networks were weaker. It is noted that the network formation by a filler in NR matrix is strongly related to the specific surface area and the self-aggregation tendency.', 'chunk_index': 24, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
