2025-07-11 21:46:09 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 2: 数据 = {'id': 'c25b1ccd-9f01-4ea2-8f76-bdeba66380ae', 'document_id': 'b183cc30-9d9a-4baa-9df9-70314ed01c98', 'content': 'article under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License, which permits use, distribution and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited. © 2022 The Authors. International Journal of Ceramic Engineering & Science published by Wiley Periodicals LLC. on behalf of the American Ceramic Society. --- The prevention of microcracking in heat-treated geopolymer composites has been an area of interest because material impermeability and higher mechanical strengths could be achieved if this microcracking was eliminated or controlled. One successful strategy that has been identified to minimize microcracking is the use of glass-forming materials dispersed in a geopolymer composite. ${}^{{28},{29}}$ The glass phase melts and permeates microcracks when exposed to high temperature, effectively filling the microcracks during the sintering process. This forms a material that is effectively "self-healing" because any additional cracks that develop could be filled by the glassy phase upon reheating. Although the inclusion of a glass-forming phase has been shown in these two papers to be beneficial, it is not yet known if the glassy phase separates uniformly or not. There has also been little investigation into different glass percentages and compositions, different alumina morphologies, and the effect of specimen size on the cracking characteristics. Therefore, the current study aims to investigate a composite of geopolymer, alumina platelets, and glass powder. The uniformity of deformation that occurs during heating will be studied, along with the effect of specimen size on micro- and macro-cracking behaviors, as well as the self-healing properties of the composite.\n## 2 | METHODOLOGY\n### 2.1 | Material synthesis', 'chunk_index': 2, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
