2025-07-11 21:46:09 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:175 - 创建分块 3: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:46:09 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 3: 数据 = {'id': '97ab2338-feb2-4d2f-8e9e-fb6170cd0d0f', 'document_id': 'b183cc30-9d9a-4baa-9df9-70314ed01c98', 'content': 'a composite of geopolymer, alumina platelets, and glass powder. The uniformity of deformation that occurs during heating will be studied, along with the effect of specimen size on micro- and macro-cracking behaviors, as well as the self-healing properties of the composite. ## 2 | METHODOLOGY ### 2.1 | Material synthesis KGP was prepared from 1.2- $\\mu \\mathrm{m}$ -sized metakaolin (BASF MetaMax from Scott Chemicals Australia Pty Ltd.) and a potassium silicate solution. Potassium silicate solution was prepared using reverse osmosis (RO) water, fumed silica $\\left( {{0.2} - {0.3\\mu }\\mathrm{m}}\\right)$ , and ${85}\\%$ assayed potassium hydroxide from Sigma-Aldrich Merck. The chemical equation for producing potassium silicate solution from ${\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}$ , deionized water, and $\\mathrm{{KOH}}$ is shown in Equation (1):\n$$ 2\\mathrm{{KOH}} + 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} + {10}{\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} \\rightarrow {\\mathrm{K}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} \\cdot 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} \\cdot {11}{\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} \\tag{1} $$\nPotassium hydroxide and fumed silica were slowly added to RO water in a stainless-steel mixing vessel to prevent flash boiling. The solution was then mixed using a magnetic stir bar for ${24}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ , as shown in Figure 1.\nMetaMAX metakaolin was then added to the potassium metasilicate solution and highly sheared at ${2000}\\mathrm{{rpm}}$ using an IKA (TM) high shear mixer for ${10}\\mathrm{\\;{min}}$ , as shown in Figure 2. The result was KGP, the chemical equation for producing KGP from metakaolin clay and potassium silicate solution is given in Equation (2):\n$$ \\left\\lbrack {{\\mathrm{K}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} + 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} + {11}{\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{O}}\\right\\rbrack + \\left\\lbrack {{\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3} \\cdot 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}}\\right\\rbrack $$', 'chunk_index': 3, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
