2025-07-11 21:46:09 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:175 - 创建分块 4: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:46:09 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 4: 数据 = {'id': 'ce23da2d-170e-41a9-aeb2-0229a3135bae', 'document_id': 'b183cc30-9d9a-4baa-9df9-70314ed01c98', 'content': 'using an IKA (TM) high shear mixer for ${10}\\mathrm{\\;{min}}$ , as shown in Figure 2. The result was KGP, the chemical equation for producing KGP from metakaolin clay and potassium silicate solution is given in Equation (2): $$ \\left\\lbrack {{\\mathrm{K}}_{2}\\mathrm{O} + 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2} + {11}{\\mathrm{H}}_{2}\\mathrm{O}}\\right\\rbrack + \\left\\lbrack {{\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3} \\cdot 2{\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}}\\right\\rbrack $$ Once KGP was mixed to homogeneity for $5\\mathrm{\\;{min}}$ and deaired on a vibrating table for $2\\mathrm{\\;{min}},{15}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\% {50\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ alumina platelets were added. ${}^{32}$ The alumina and KGP were highly sheared at ${2000}\\mathrm{{rpm}}$ to homogeneity for $5\\mathrm{\\;{min}}$ and deaired for $2\\mathrm{\\;{min}}$ . Finally, ${35}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ Uroboros System 96 glass frit was added to the $\\mathrm{{KGP}} - {\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$ mixture, highly sheared at ${2000}\\mathrm{{rpm}}$ for $5\\mathrm{\\;{min}}$ , and deaired for $2\\mathrm{\\;{min}}$ . The resulting composite was placed in three different sized cylindrical molds.\nSamples and molds were placed in a ${100}\\%$ relative humidity, room temperature curing chamber for 7 days.\nTABLE 2 Example dimensions of ${50}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ potassium metakaolin-based geopolymer (KGP)-35 wt% glass powder-15 wt% alumina platelets\n<table><tr><td>Cylinder size</td><td>Diameter (mm)</td><td>Height (mm)</td><td>Unfired weight (g)</td></tr><tr><td>Large</td><td>38.7</td><td>36.3</td><td>83.9</td></tr><tr><td>Medium</td><td>21.1</td><td>37.6</td><td>25.8</td></tr><tr><td>Small</td><td>12.2</td><td>35.9</td><td>8.4</td></tr></table>\nAfter 1 week of curing, the samples were demolded and allowed to bench dry for ${48}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ . Examples of the sample dimensions are shown in Table 2 and Figure 3. Three sizes were chosen to study the scalability and impact of the aspect ratio.\n### 2.2 | Heat treatments', 'chunk_index': 4, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
