2025-07-11 21:46:09 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:175 - 创建分块 7: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:46:09 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 7: 数据 = {'id': '3b6f6e7f-56ef-4331-8ae6-4cf5d9282d85', 'document_id': 'b183cc30-9d9a-4baa-9df9-70314ed01c98', 'content': '(6). Bulk density</td></tr><tr><td>${\\rho }_{\\text{AAM Grain }} = \\frac{{W}_{\\text{Dry }}}{{V}_{\\text{Matrix }}} = \\frac{{W}_{\\text{Dry }} \\times {\\rho }_{\\text{Water }}}{\\left( {W}_{\\text{Dry }} - {W}_{\\text{Sub }}\\right) }$</td><td>Equation (7). Grain density</td></tr><tr><td>Open porosity $= \\frac{{V}_{\\text{Open pores }}}{{V}_{\\text{Bulk }}} = \\frac{{W}_{\\text{Sat }} - {W}_{\\text{Dry }}}{{W}_{\\text{Sat }} - {W}_{\\text{Sub }}}$</td><td>Equation (8). Open porosity</td></tr></table> ### 2.4 | Thermal analysis A Panalytical Empyrean X-ray diffractometer was used to collect diffraction patterns of powdered samples and starting reagents. Tests were conducted at ${40}\\mathrm{{kV}},{40}\\mathrm{{mA}}$ , a step size of ${0.02}^{ \\circ }{2\\theta }$ , and a measurement time of ${60}\\mathrm{\\;s}/$ step. The $\\mathrm{X}$ -ray source was ${\\mathrm{{CuK}}}_{\\alpha }$ with a nickel filter monochromator and an approximate wavelength of ${1.54Å}$ . The results were compared to the International Centre for Diffraction Data PDF4+ database.\n## 3 | RESULTS\n### 3.1 Heat-treated samples\nGeopolymer samples that were heated to ${300}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ remained as permeable as room temperature samples, as seen in Figure 3. However, heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ produced a uniform surface glaze, as shown in Figure 4. No warping occurred in any sample. The largest size samples developed a hairline crack after heating to ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ , as shown in Figure 5.\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_165_134_663_339_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_165_134_663_339_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 4 Geopolymer samples after heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for $5\\mathrm{\\;h}$ with a heating and cooling rate of ${1}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}/\\mathrm{{min}}$\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_184_626_625_303_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_4_184_626_625_303_0.jpg)', 'chunk_index': 7, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
