2025-07-11 21:46:09 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 13: 数据 = {'id': '4912109a-002c-4b6e-87ba-996a865eb571', 'document_id': 'b183cc30-9d9a-4baa-9df9-70314ed01c98', 'content': 'individual phases with no chemical reactions taking place, as shown in Figure 17. ![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_7_339_134_1096_812_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_7_339_134_1096_812_0.jpg) FIG URE 14 Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) micrographs of geopolymer composites using a backscattered electron detector. As cured (A), after exposure to ${300}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ (B), ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ (C), and ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ (D). ![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_7_337_1096_1098_526_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_7_337_1096_1098_526_0.jpg) FIG URE 15 Energy dispersive X-ray spectra (EDS) map of geopolymer composite after heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for 20 h using heating/cooling rates of ${1}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}/\\mathrm{{min}}$ . Brighter areas contained more of the specified element\nPatterns of heated geopolymer composites are shown in Figure 18. Heat treatment of ASH-G samples to ${300}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ and ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ did not alter the overall crystallinity or phase fraction of the composites. However, after heating to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for both 5 and ${20}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ , the diffractograms indicated the formation of a new phase. Analysis of the crystalline peaks indicated that the new phase that formed during high-temperature treatment was leucite, and this was indexed using powder diffraction file PDF 00-031-0967. ${}^{36}$ What is unclear from this result is where the leucite was forming, from within the glass phase, from the geopolymer, or from a reaction between one of the phases present. In order to determine the origin of the leucite, individual phases were heated to ${900}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ for ${20}\\mathrm{\\;h}$ , and the XRD results were compared, as shown in Figures 18 and 19.\n![0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_8_129_134_734_620_0.jpg](images/0197448d-ce32-7a6e-bb80-13bab7cf1e87_8_129_134_734_620_0.jpg)', 'chunk_index': 13, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
