2025-07-11 21:46:10 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:175 - 创建分块 5: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 21:46:10 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 5: 数据 = {'id': '3e88f490-c193-411e-a061-a48d6e9b4836', 'document_id': '7ff3822c-812a-43ee-8698-1aa9534912ec', 'content': "Griffith's principle, specimens containing larger pre-existing crack would exhibit low compressive strength. The use of ${12}\\mathrm{\\;{mol}}/\\mathrm{l}$ $\\mathrm{{NaOH}}$ solution resulted in smooth surface, less existing crack, and less existence of unreacted fly ash particles. Therefore, this concentration used as alkaline activator for the preparation of fly ash based geopolymer-mullite composites. ![01973e1a-dfde-72a9-84ae-b84e3d3bb8ca_4_380_834_869_529_0.jpg](images/01973e1a-dfde-72a9-84ae-b84e3d3bb8ca_4_380_834_869_529_0.jpg) The compressive strength of ${20} - {60}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ mullite added geopolymer composite is given in Figure 4. It showed that by adding just ${20}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ of mullite the compressive strength of the geopolymer was increased significantly to ${44}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ , i.e. three times stronger than the fly ash-geopolymer without addition. By adding ${40}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ of mullite, a remarkable improvement in compressive strength, ${71}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ , was achieved. However, at 60 wt% of mullite addition, the compressive strength decreased to ${58}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ . It can be concluded that ${40}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ is the optimum level of mullite addition into fly ash-based geopolymer. microstructures, as shown in Figure 8. Ina composite with 20 wt% addition, small mullite crystals could be observed within the matrix of geopolymer, associated with an improvement in compressive strength. At ${40}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ addition, more mullite crystals with longer and larger needle-like shape were detected. Small needlelike structure and interlocking of mullite crystals were proposed to be the key factor for achieving high strength (Carty and Senapati, 1998). With its high aspect ratio, mullite crystal could effectively help resist crack propagation and successfully reinforce the matrix in composite system. As a result, the compressive strength was the highest with such microstructure. However, even though the mullite crystal was found overa broader area in the case of ${60}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ addition, but compressive strength in this condition was not as high as at ${40}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ .", 'chunk_index': 5, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
