2025-07-11 21:46:41 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 3: 数据 = {'id': '36251507-18a0-4195-aa99-2a466f2c23ee', 'document_id': '8f0e4010-d70a-4f47-9129-b82d8760cbc2', 'content': 'strength ${}^{17}$ . Potassium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${6.4}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ rice stem yielded ${18.45}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ three-point flexure strength ${}^{18}$ . Potassium-based geopolymer reinforced with 30 wt% alkali-treated fique fibers yielded ${11.4}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{19}$ . Sodium-based geopolymer reinforced with ${5.5}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ of unidirectional untreated malva resulted in ${31.5}\\mathrm{{MPa}}$ four-point flexure strength ${}^{20}$ .  Presently, we found no published work on metakaolin-based geopolymer reinforced with bamboo fibers.', 'chunk_index': 3, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
