2025-07-11 22:04:05 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 2: 数据 = {'id': '2cdad679-99b2-41bd-94c7-f76bb8e279b0', 'document_id': 'd36b7122-2414-41cc-bb70-d36713287425', 'content': "compound viscosity is increased substantially due to strong silica-silica interactions, ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 8\\right\\rbrack }$ and the production of these conventional fillers is highly energy-consuming. Thus, alternative fillers from renewable resources are of considerable interest to improve the properties of rubber while improving sustainability and green aspects of the rubber life cycle. In recent years, silica from natural sources has attracted attention as an alternative reinforcing filler in natural and synthetic rubber, because of low cost, good mechanical properties, dimensional stability, and environmental issues. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack 9\\right\\rbrack }$ Types of natural fillers exploited in rubber composites include fly ash (FA), ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {10}\\right\\rbrack }$ rice husk ash (RHA), ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {11}\\right\\rbrack }$ oil palm ash (OPA), ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {12}\\right\\rbrack }$ bagasse fiber ash (BFA), ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {13}\\right\\rbrack }$ cellulose fiber, ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {14}\\right\\rbrack }$ coconut shell powder (CSP), ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {15}\\right\\rbrack }$ and lignin. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {16}\\right\\rbrack }$ The FA is a byproduct from the combustion of pulverized coal in electric power generating plants. It is a potential alternative filler in rubber materials with nearly ${40} - {50}\\mathrm{{wt}}\\%$ silica content. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {10}\\right\\rbrack }$ In addition, FA contains various chemical elements, including aluminum, iron, calcium, magnesium, sulfur, sodium, potassium, and carbon. On the other hand, RHA filler has also been tested in natural rubber compounds. ${}^{\\left\\lbrack {17}\\right\\rbrack }$ It was found that the incorporation of RHA significantly affected cure characteristics and mechanical properties of NR composites. That is, RHA caused faster curing and increased Young's modulus, tensile strength and other related strength properties. In addition, OPA filler was also used in rubber compounds, and tensile strength and elongation at break improved by about ${16}\\%$ and ${7.", 'chunk_index': 2, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
