2025-07-11 22:04:05 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 9: 数据 = {'id': '008812b6-2fcb-405d-b16c-e473a8ea8912', 'document_id': 'd36b7122-2414-41cc-bb70-d36713287425', 'content': 'IL, USA). The morphology of geopolymer particles was also imaged by scanning electron microscopy (SEM, FEI-Quanta 400, Jeol Ltd., Tokyo, Japan). Furthermore, the density of geopolymer was gravimetrically measured, and its $\\mathrm{{pH}}$ was determined by the procedure described in ISO 10523: 1994. ### 2.3 | Analysis of FA and GP The chemical compositions of GP and FA were characterized by X-ray fluorescence spectrometry (XRF, PW2400, Philips, Elisabeth, the Netherlands). Each powder was first dried to constant weight in a hot air oven at about ${100}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ over 14 hr. The sample was then treated in a muffle furnace by heating from 50 to $1,{000}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ . It was then mixed with a binder (i.e., WAX C) in the weight ratio 2:1 and then compressed to a thin sheet. Finally, the sheet samples were characterized by XRF.\n### 2.4 | Preparation of NR/geopolymer composites\nNatural rubber/geopolymer composites were prepared by dry mixing at room temperature using a two-roll mill. The compounding formulation and mixing schedule with ${13}\\mathrm{\\;{min}}$ total mixing time are shown in Table 2. It is noted that the compounds and vulcanizates with various geopolymer loadings (0,10,20,30, or40phr)are here labeled as gum NR, NR-GP10, NR-GP20, NR-GP30, and NR-GP40, respectively. The rubber compound was then sheeted out and conditioned at room temperature for ${12}\\mathrm{{hr}}$ before vulcanizing and testing. It is noted that also neat fly ash was used to prepare FA/NR composites for a comparison purpose. The FA particles were prepared in a similar manner as the geopolymer, by ball milling for ${48}\\mathrm{{hr}}$ .\n### 2.5 | Cure characterization', 'chunk_index': 9, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
