2025-07-11 22:04:05 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 10: 数据 = {'id': '7f1318f5-a5c4-48e4-97ec-3f7cde2290de', 'document_id': 'd36b7122-2414-41cc-bb70-d36713287425', 'content': 'at room temperature for ${12}\\mathrm{{hr}}$ before vulcanizing and testing. It is noted that also neat fly ash was used to prepare FA/NR composites for a comparison purpose. The FA particles were prepared in a similar manner as the geopolymer, by ball milling for ${48}\\mathrm{{hr}}$ . ### 2.5 | Cure characterization The tensile properties of the GP/NR and FA/NR composites were determined using a universal tensile testing machine (Tinius Olsen, model 10ST, Salfords, England) with a crosshead speed of ${200}\\mathrm{\\;{mm}}/\\mathrm{{min}}$ according to ISO 527. The dumbbell shape used was ISO 527 (type 5A). The stress-strain curves were recorded, and tensile strength and elongation at break were estimated from these curves.\n### 2.7 | Dynamic properties\nDynamic properties in terms of storage modulus $\\left( {\\mathrm{G}}^{\\prime }\\right)$ were investigated using RPA 2000 (Alpha Technologies, Akron, USA). The strain sweep from 0.56% to 500% was performed at ${80}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ at the constant $1\\mathrm{\\;{Hz}}$ frequency.\n### 2.8 | Thermal properties\nThermal stability of the GP/NR and FA/NR samples was characterized by thermogravimetric analysis (TGA; STA 6000, Perkin Elmer Inc., Norwalk, CT, USA). A sample of approximately ${20}\\mathrm{{mg}}$ was placed in a ceramic pan and then heated at ${10}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}/\\mathrm{{min}}$ rate across the temperature range from 30 to ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ , under nitrogen atmosphere.\nTABLE 3 Physical properties of fly ash and geopolymer particles\n<table><tr><td>Properties</td><td>Fly ash</td><td>Geopolymer</td></tr><tr><td>Mean particle size $\\left( {\\mu \\mathrm{m}}\\right)$</td><td>13.5</td><td>9.5</td></tr><tr><td>Density $\\left( {\\mathrm{g}/{\\mathrm{{cm}}}^{3}}\\right)$</td><td>1.04</td><td>1.05</td></tr><tr><td>pH</td><td>12.4</td><td>12.0</td></tr></table>', 'chunk_index': 10, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
