2025-07-11 22:04:05 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 11: 数据 = {'id': 'b2455243-3e9c-46cf-b25d-bf24f8982ef9', 'document_id': 'd36b7122-2414-41cc-bb70-d36713287425', 'content': 'of approximately ${20}\\mathrm{{mg}}$ was placed in a ceramic pan and then heated at ${10}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}/\\mathrm{{min}}$ rate across the temperature range from 30 to ${600}^{ \\circ }\\mathrm{C}$ , under nitrogen atmosphere. TABLE 3 Physical properties of fly ash and geopolymer particles <table><tr><td>Properties</td><td>Fly ash</td><td>Geopolymer</td></tr><tr><td>Mean particle size $\\left( {\\mu \\mathrm{m}}\\right)$</td><td>13.5</td><td>9.5</td></tr><tr><td>Density $\\left( {\\mathrm{g}/{\\mathrm{{cm}}}^{3}}\\right)$</td><td>1.04</td><td>1.05</td></tr><tr><td>pH</td><td>12.4</td><td>12.0</td></tr></table> ### 2.9 | Morphological characterization\nThe morphological properties of GP/NR and FA/NR samples were characterized by scanning electron microscopy (FEI-Quanta 400, Jeol Ltd., Tokyo, Japan). The specimens were first cryogenically fractured to create fresh cross-sectional surfaces that were gold coated by sputtering under vacuum before imaging by SEM. A metallographic optical microscope (Carl Zeiss Microscopy GmbH, Oberkochen, Germany) was also used to examine the morphologies of the GP/NR and FA/ NR samples. The samples were fast cut with a razor blade to create smooth sample surfaces before the optical microscopy.\n## 3 RESULTS AND DISCUSSION\n### 3.1 | Characteristics of geopolymer and fly ash particles\nFigure 2 shows the particle size distributions of geopolymer and fly ash. It can be seen that the FA had a narrower size distribution than the GP but with larger ${13.5\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ mean particle size than the ${9.5\\mu }\\mathrm{m}$ of GP (Table 3). It is also seen that both FA and GP had similar pH and density (Table 3). Table 4 shows the chemical compositions of FA and GP. It is seen that these two fillers had otherwise similar chemical compositions, but the geopolymer had more silicon dioxide $\\left( {\\mathrm{{SiO}}}_{2}\\right)$ . Also, some compounds were only found in GP, including phosphorus pentoxide, manganese oxide, barium oxide, sodium oxide, and zirconium oxide.', 'chunk_index': 11, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
