2025-07-11 22:04:05 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 18: 数据 = {'id': '13372017-b4f8-4d2c-a059-471b56679fe1', 'document_id': 'd36b7122-2414-41cc-bb70-d36713287425', 'content': 'of fly ash (Figure 3), and it gives larger agglomerates with poorer distribution than the GP (Figures 6 and 7). Furthermore, the GP/NR (10 phr) vulcanizate exhibited higher delta torque than the gum NR vulcanizate or the NR/FA (10 phr). This indicates higher cross-link density in the composite with GP. FIGURE 4 Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy spectra of geopolymer and fly ash particles [Colour figure can be viewed at wileyonlinelibrary.com]\n### 3.2 | Geopolymerization and chemical composition of geopolymer and fly ash particles\n![01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_4_636_1723_1005_472_0.jpg](images/01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_4_636_1723_1005_472_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 3 Scanning electron microscopy micrographs of (a) geopolymer and (b) fly ash particles\n<table><tr><td>$\\mathbf{{Wavenumber}}\\left( {\\mathbf{{cm}}}^{-1}\\right)$</td><td>Assignment</td><td>$\\mathbf{{Ref}.}$</td></tr><tr><td>681</td><td>Vibration of ${\\mathrm{{Al}}}_{2}{\\mathrm{O}}_{3}$</td><td>[24]</td></tr><tr><td>1007</td><td>Al-O-Al stretching</td><td>[24]</td></tr><tr><td>1086 and 1100</td><td>Asymmetric stretching vibrations of Si-O-T bonds (T—tetrahedral Al or Si)</td><td>[26]</td></tr><tr><td>1434, 1625, 3445, and 3452</td><td>Stretching vibration of $- \\mathrm{{OH}}$ bonds</td><td>[25]</td></tr></table>\nTABLE 5 Assignments of the peaks of infrared spectra in Figure 3\n### 3.3 | Cure characteristics\n![01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_5_910_484_728_608_0.jpg](images/01974484-c8d5-72ac-a6d1-acf6a850ed04_5_910_484_728_608_0.jpg)\nFIGURE 5 Cure curves for the gum and the geopolymer (GP)- or fly ash (FA)-filled natural rubber vulcanizates, with various GP loadings or 10 phr FA', 'chunk_index': 18, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.T