2025-07-11 22:04:06 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:175 - 创建分块 2: 数据键 = ['id', 'document_id', 'content', 'chunk_index', 'chunk_metadata']
2025-07-11 22:04:06 | INFO     | db.repositories.knowledge_repository:create_chunks:176 - 创建分块 2: 数据 = {'id': 'e70d7ea3-2884-402b-8246-c33ea2929a19', 'document_id': '58b1d2d2-05dd-4b74-98c0-d84578c57cec', 'content': 'et al., 2013; Abdulkareem et al., 2014; Bagheri and Nazari, 2014; Abdollahnejad et al., 2015; Embong et al., 2015). Therefore, engineering class $\\mathrm{C}$ fly ash based geopolymer for high compressive strength applications is a great challenge. In order to realize that, it might need to be reinforced or composited. --- Fly ash used in this study was collected from Mae Moh power plant, Lampang province, Thailand, while an industrial grade mullite powder was purchased from a local supplier in Thailand. Figure 1 presents SEM pictures of raw materials. Fly ash particle can be seen consist of spherical vitreous particles and mullite powder has irregular shape. Figure 2 presents the X-ray diffraction analysis result of raw materials. TABLE 1 presents chemical composition of fly ash and mullite as detected by X-ray Fluorescence. The chemical composition of fly ash is classified to class $\\mathrm{C}$ as specified in ASTM C-168. The particle distribution of fly ash and mullite powder was measured by laser diffraction analysis (Malvern Instrument Mastersizer, 2000) as presented in TABLE 2. In this study, a mixture of chemical-grade sodium hydroxide solution and commercial sodium silicate was used as the alkaline activator.\n![01973e1a-dfde-72a9-84ae-b84e3d3bb8ca_2_212_1095_1193_410_0.jpg](images/01973e1a-dfde-72a9-84ae-b84e3d3bb8ca_2_212_1095_1193_410_0.jpg)\nFigure 1. SEM pictures of raw materials\n![01973e1a-dfde-72a9-84ae-b84e3d3bb8ca_2_437_1593_766_507_0.jpg](images/01973e1a-dfde-72a9-84ae-b84e3d3bb8ca_2_437_1593_766_507_0.jpg)\nFigure 2. X-ray diffractogram of raw materials\n## Sample Preparation', 'chunk_index': 2, 'chunk_metadata': {'strategy': 'semantic', 'type': 'ContentType.TEXT', 'headings': [], 'page_number': [1], 'extra': None}}
